WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.568
Learn to compare and order fractions with like denominators by using pictorial

00:00:05.568 --> 00:00:10.041
representations and finding equivalent fractions using the lowest common denominator

00:00:10.041 --> 00:00:14.067
(lcd) and provide examples of where fractions are used

00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:21.224
Which fraction is greater: 2/4 or 3/4? The answer is 3/4. With equal denominators,

00:00:21.224 --> 00:00:24.403
the larger numerator gives the larger fraction.

00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:31.792
Two ribbons are 2/8 m and 7/8 m long. Which is longer? Pause and solve it in your

00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:32.515
exercise book.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:38.167
The answer is 7/8. With equal denominators compare numerators.
